\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Dual-backbone RT-DETR and the inherited Feature Alignment Module. At each pyramid level, RGB and IR features jointly predict 18 offset components and nine modulation masks; DCNv2 then transforms the IR feature before additive fusion. In the final data path, training-only Modal Dropout zero-pads the missing input channels while preserving the four-channel interface. The FAM is the starting point inherited from the preceding Computer Vision project, not a new architecture introduced by this thesis.}}{9}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fam-architecture}{{2.1}{9}{Dual-backbone RT-DETR and the inherited Feature Alignment Module. At each pyramid level, RGB and IR features jointly predict 18 offset components and nine modulation masks; DCNv2 then transforms the IR feature before additive fusion. In the final data path, training-only Modal Dropout zero-pads the missing input channels while preserving the four-channel interface. The FAM is the starting point inherited from the preceding Computer Vision project, not a new architecture introduced by this thesis}{figure.caption.11}{}}
\newlabel{fig:fam-architecture@cref}{{[figure][1][2]2.1}{[1][8][]9}{}{}{}}
